@startuml Episode Management Workflow
!theme plain
title SABER Episode Management Workflow - Current Implementation

actor Client
participant "AgentUnderTest" as Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "SessionRestAPI" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI" as MCP
participant "BenchmarkManager" as BM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM
participant "PolicyManager" as PM
participant "EvaluationManager" as EVAL_M
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC

== Client-Side Benchmark Orchestration ==

Client -> REST: GET /api/v1/tasks
REST -> SM: get_benchmark_info()
SM -> BM: get_benchmark_info()
BM --> SM: BenchmarkInfo
SM --> REST: BenchmarkInfo
REST -> Client: BenchmarkInfo (with tasks & episode_attempts)

note right of Client
Client receives complete benchmark information:
- List of all tasks with episode_attempts
- Total episodes across all tasks
- Client decides task order and orchestration
end note

== Episode Initialization (Async) ==

Client -> REST: POST /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes?task_id=malware_analysis_001
REST -> SM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
SM -> BM: get_task(task_id) and get_single_episode_task(task_id)
BM --> SM: Task (with environment, allowed_executors, episode_config, etc.)

== Task Configuration & Episode Setup (Under Global Lock) ==

SM -> SM: acquire _episode_creation_lock (global)
SM -> SM: create Episode object (state=CREATING)
SM -> EM: add_episode_to_session(session_id, episode)
EM --> SM: episode tracked

SM -> SM: session.add_creating_episode(episode_id)
SM -> SM: handle dependency resolution with retry if task.depends_on_task_id

SM -> EM_EXEC: configure_for_task_async(episode_id, task, session_id, target_episode_id)
EM_EXEC -> EM_EXEC: create_episode_environment_async (NO health checks)
EM_EXEC --> SM: Docker containers starting

SM -> SM: session.move_to_active_episode(episode_id)
SM -> SM: release _episode_creation_lock

== Background Finalization (runs concurrently) ==

SM -> SM: spawn _finalize_episode_creation background task

note right of SM
Background finalization (with semaphore limit):
1. wait_for_episode_healthy() - health checks
2. prompt_generator.render_agent_prompts_for_task()
3. policy_manager.set_episode_policy(episode_id, session_id, prompt)
4. episode_manager.configure_for_task(episode_id, task)
5. copy_initial_files_to_episode()
6. evaluation_manager.configure_for_task(task)
7. mark_episode_ready(episode_id)
end note

SM --> REST: EpisodeCreateResponse (state=CREATING)
REST -> Client: {episode_id, task_id, session_id, state="creating", message, episode_context, attached_to_episode_id}

== Client Polls for Episode Status ==

Client -> REST: GET /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}/status
REST -> SM: get_episode_status(session_id, episode_id)
SM -> EM: get_episode_by_id(episode_id)
EM --> SM: Episode
SM --> REST: EpisodeStatusResponse
REST -> Client: {state="ready", is_ready=true} (after finalization completes)

== Policy and Task Context Retrieval ==

Client -> REST: GET /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}/policy
REST -> SM: get_policy(session_id, episode_id)
SM -> PM: get_policy(episode_id)
PM --> SM: PolicyDocument(prompt)
SM --> REST: PolicyResponse
REST -> Client: {prompt: "...", domain: "..."}

Client -> REST: GET /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}/task
REST -> SM: get_episode_task(episode_id)
SM -> EM: get_episode_by_id(episode_id)
EM --> SM: Episode
SM -> BM: get_task(episode.task_id)
BM --> SM: Task
SM --> REST: EpisodeTaskResponse
REST -> Client: task_context

== Agent Initialization & MCP Setup ==

Client -> Agent: initialize(task_context + policy)
Agent --> Client: ready

Client -> MCP: connect(session_id, episode_id, orchestration_env via headers)
MCP -> MCP: _get_headers() and validate SABER context
MCP -> SM: validate session exists
SM --> MCP: session_context
MCP -> Client: connected

Client -> MCP: list_tools()
MCP -> MCP: _register_dynamic_tools() for episode
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: get_executors_for_episode()
EM_EXEC -> MCP: dynamic tool schemas + end_episode tool
MCP -> Client: available_tools[]

== RL Episode Step Execution ==

Agent -> Agent: decide_next_action()
Agent -> Client: tool_request("bash", {command: "file malware.exe"})
Client -> MCP: call_tool("bash", {command: "file malware.exe"})
MCP -> MCP: extract headers and validate session/episode context
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, episode_id, action)

SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action, context)
EM_EXEC --> SM: CommandResult

SM -> EM: step(episode_id, action, command_result)

== EpisodeManager Step Processing ==

EM -> EM: get_episode_by_id(episode_id)
EM -> EM: create_step(episode, action, command_result)
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM -> EM: add_step(episode)
EM --> SM: StepResult(step, should_terminate=False, termination_reason=None)

note right of EM
StepResult always returns should_terminate=False:
- step: Step object with action/response
- should_terminate: always False (no server-side termination)
- termination_reason: always None

Episode termination is now client-side responsibility
Server only tracks steps for analysis and evaluation
end note

SM -> MCP: CommandResult
MCP -> Client: mcp_result
Client -> Agent: execution_result

== Episode Continuation ==

Agent -> Agent: process_result()
Agent -> Agent: plan_next_action()

note right of Agent
Agent continues episode execution.
Client is responsible for:
- Tracking step counts against max_steps
- Deciding when to terminate episodes
- Managing episode attempts per task
- Orchestrating task progression
end note

== Episode Termination ==

alt Agent completes task
    Agent -> Client: end_episode_request(submission="flag{found}")
    Client -> MCP: call_tool("end_episode", {submission: "flag{found}"})
    MCP -> MCP: validate headers (session_id, episode_id, orchestration_env)
    MCP -> SM: end_episode(session_id, episode_id, "agent_completed", submission)
    SM -> EM: end_episode(episode_id, "agent_completed", submission)
    EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED
    EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = "agent_completed"
    EM -> EM: move to completed_episodes
    EM --> SM: Episode
    SM -> SM: session.complete_episode(episode_id)
    SM -> EM_EXEC: cleanup_episode(episode_id)
    SM --> MCP: EpisodeEndResponse (evaluation_result=None - client evaluates)
    MCP -> Client: episode_ended
else Client terminates episode (max steps/timeout)
    Client -> REST: DELETE /api/v1/session/{session_id}/episodes/{episode_id}
    REST -> SM: end_episode(session_id, episode_id, "client_terminated", None)
    SM -> EM: end_episode(episode_id, "client_terminated")
    EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED
    EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = "client_terminated"
    EM --> SM: Episode
    SM -> SM: session.complete_episode(episode_id)
    SM -> EM_EXEC: cleanup_episode(episode_id)
    SM --> REST: EpisodeEndResponse (evaluation_result=None)
    REST -> Client: episode_ended
end

== Client-Side Orchestration (Multiple Episodes) ==

note over Client
Client handles complete benchmark orchestration:
1. Gets BenchmarkInfo from /api/v1/tasks
2. Creates session via POST /api/v1/session
3. For each task in benchmark:
   - Creates episodes up to episode_attempts limit
   - Tracks step counts and enforces max_steps
   - Handles timeouts and termination conditions
   - Manages dependency resolution for attached episodes
   - Decides task progression and retry logic
4. Retrieves evaluations via /api/v1/session/{id}/evaluations
5. Terminates session when benchmark complete
end note

== Session Cleanup ==

Client -> MCP: disconnect()
MCP -> SM: automatic session cleanup on disconnect
Client -> REST: DELETE /api/v1/session/{session_id}
REST -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
SM -> EM: cleanup_session_episodes(session_id)
EM -> EM: end any remaining active episodes
EM -> EM: cleanup session_episodes mapping
SM -> EM_EXEC: cleanup_session_environments(session_id)
SM -> PM: cleanup_episode_policies(session_id)
SM --> REST: SessionTerminateResponse
REST -> Client: HTTP 200 OK

note over Client, Agent
**Current Implementation Architecture**

**Clear Separation of Concerns:**
- REST API: Session lifecycle, episode management, policy/task access, evaluation results
- MCP API: Tool execution only with header-based session/episode context
- Client: Complete benchmark orchestration, episode management, AND evaluation
- EpisodeManager: RL-style episode tracking without server-side termination
- Agent: Task execution using MCP tools, can trigger completion via end_episode tool

**Key Implementation Details:**
- No server-side benchmark orchestration or task queues
- Client-side step counting and episode termination logic
- Server tracks steps for analysis but doesn't enforce limits
- CLIENT-SIDE evaluation via scorer registry (server stores results only)
- Episode-specific policy management via PolicyManager
- Sessions support multiple concurrent/sequential episodes
- Task dependency resolution with episode attachment
- Fail-fast design with no backwards compatibility
- Header-based MCP context: X-SABER-Session-ID, X-SABER-Episode-ID, X-SABER-Orchestration-Env
- Dynamic tool registration based on task executor configuration

**Updated Episode Lifecycle (Async):**
1. Client gets tasks via /api/v1/tasks and orchestrates execution
2. Episode created in CREATING state (returns immediately)
3. Background finalization: health checks, prompts, file copies, config
4. Client polls GET .../status until state=READY
5. Agent executes actions via MCP tools with header context
6. Server tracks steps but doesn't auto-terminate
7. Episode ends via end_episode tool (agent) or DELETE endpoint (client)
8. Episode cleanup (Docker containers, networks)
9. CLIENT performs evaluation and submits results
10. Client manages task progression, retries, and benchmark completion
end note

@enduml
